---
toolSlug: cors-debugger
permalink: /tools/cors-debugger/
---

<div class="tool-group">
  <label for="cors-origin">Origin URL <span class="cors-hint">(your frontend)</span></label>
  <input type="url" id="cors-origin" placeholder="https://app.example.com" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
</div>

<div class="tool-group">
  <label for="cors-target">Target URL <span class="cors-hint">(the API you're calling)</span></label>
  <input type="url" id="cors-target" placeholder="https://api.example.com/v1/data" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
</div>

<div class="tool-row" style="gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
  <div class="tool-group" style="flex:1;min-width:160px;">
    <label for="cors-method">HTTP Method</label>
    <select id="cors-method">
      <option value="GET">GET</option>
      <option value="POST" selected>POST</option>
      <option value="PUT">PUT</option>
      <option value="DELETE">DELETE</option>
      <option value="PATCH">PATCH</option>
      <option value="OPTIONS">OPTIONS</option>
    </select>
  </div>
  <div class="tool-group" style="flex:0 0 auto;align-self:flex-end;">
    <label class="cors-toggle-label">
      <input type="checkbox" id="cors-credentials">
      <span class="cors-toggle-track"><span class="cors-toggle-thumb"></span></span>
      Send credentials (cookies)
    </label>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="tool-group">
  <label for="cors-headers">Custom Request Headers <span class="cors-hint">(one per line)</span></label>
  <textarea id="cors-headers" rows="3" placeholder="Authorization&#10;Content-Type: application/json&#10;X-Custom-Header" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off"></textarea>
</div>

<div class="tool-row">
  <button class="btn btn--primary" id="cors-analyze-btn">Analyze</button>
  <button class="btn" id="cors-example-btn">Try example</button>
  <button class="btn" id="cors-clear-btn">Clear</button>
</div>

<div id="cors-empty" class="cors-empty-msg">Enter your origin and target URLs, then click "Analyze" to diagnose CORS behavior.</div>

<div id="cors-results" style="display:none;">

  <!-- Is this a CORS request? -->
  <div class="cors-section" id="cors-is-cors"></div>

  <!-- Preflight needed? -->
  <div class="cors-section" id="cors-preflight"></div>

  <!-- Preflight request -->
  <div class="cors-section" id="cors-preflight-req" style="display:none;"></div>

  <!-- Required server headers -->
  <div class="cors-section" id="cors-server-headers"></div>

  <!-- Common mistakes -->
  <div class="cors-section" id="cors-mistakes" style="display:none;"></div>

  <!-- Server config generator -->
  <div class="cors-section" id="cors-configs">
    <h3 class="cors-section-title">Server Configuration Generator</h3>
    <div class="tool-options" role="group" aria-label="Server platform" id="cors-platform-tabs">
      <button class="tool-option active" data-platform="express" aria-pressed="true">Express.js</button>
      <button class="tool-option" data-platform="nginx" aria-pressed="false">nginx</button>
      <button class="tool-option" data-platform="cloudflare" aria-pressed="false">CF Worker</button>
      <button class="tool-option" data-platform="flask" aria-pressed="false">Flask</button>
      <button class="tool-option" data-platform="apigateway" aria-pressed="false">API Gateway</button>
      <button class="tool-option" data-platform="apache" aria-pressed="false">Apache</button>
    </div>
    <div class="output-area" style="position:relative;">
      <button class="btn btn--copy" id="cors-copy-config" aria-label="Copy configuration">Copy</button>
      <pre id="cors-config-output" aria-label="Server configuration"></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<hr style="margin:2rem 0;border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border,#2a2a3a);">

<!-- CORS Cheat Sheet -->
<details class="cors-cheatsheet">
  <summary class="cors-cheatsheet-summary">CORS Cheat Sheet</summary>
  <div class="cors-cheatsheet-body">
    <div class="cors-cheatsheet-section">
      <h4>Simple vs. Preflighted Requests</h4>
      <p>A <strong>simple request</strong> uses GET, HEAD, or POST with only CORS-safelisted headers (Accept, Accept-Language, Content-Language, Content-Type with text/plain, multipart/form-data, or application/x-www-form-urlencoded). Everything else triggers a <strong>preflight</strong> OPTIONS request.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cors-cheatsheet-section">
      <h4>Credentialed Requests</h4>
      <p>When sending cookies or auth headers cross-origin, the server must return <code>Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true</code> and <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin</code> must be a specific origin, not <code>*</code>. The browser will block the response otherwise.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cors-cheatsheet-section">
      <h4>Wildcard Restrictions</h4>
      <p><code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *</code> cannot be used with credentials. <code>Access-Control-Allow-Headers: *</code> and <code>Access-Control-Allow-Methods: *</code> are only supported in non-credentialed requests (and not by all browsers).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cors-cheatsheet-section">
      <h4>Preflight Caching</h4>
      <p>Use <code>Access-Control-Max-Age</code> to cache preflight responses. Chrome caps at 7200s (2h), Firefox at 86400s (24h). A value of <code>-1</code> disables caching (useful for debugging).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cors-cheatsheet-section">
      <h4>Exposed Headers</h4>
      <p>By default, only CORS-safelisted response headers are accessible to JavaScript. To expose custom headers (e.g., <code>X-Request-Id</code>, <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code>), the server must send <code>Access-Control-Expose-Headers</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cors-cheatsheet-section">
      <h4>Common Gotchas</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>CORS headers must come from the <strong>target server</strong>, not the origin server.</li>
        <li>Redirects during preflight will cause a CORS failure in most browsers.</li>
        <li>The <code>Origin</code> header is sent by the browser automatically; you cannot override it via JavaScript.</li>
        <li>Opaque responses (no-cors mode) succeed but the body/headers are inaccessible to JS.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<style>
